we are taking calls at 6 1 7 8 3 0 47 50  we will take our next call from the 9 1  7 area code New York City caller what's  your name and where are you calling from  today I'm actually calling from Los  Angeles my name is Matt Matt what's on  your mind today I just wanted to ask  about the ideological position of the  left now that we're into trumpism and  the trump presidency do you see the  Trump presidency  consolidating the left's ideology and  you know through a resistance or  something like that  or do you see a further sort of  fracturing and splintering with the  centrist left the regressive left is  there such a thing as a cohesive left  anymore now that we're so out of power  and yeah in Trump's America so listen  there's to it there's not a there's not  a fixed answer to this so there's sort  of two forces that are impacting the  left right now one is mostly unanimous  sentiment that this is a disaster that  whatever your view about hillary clinton  was the idea that Trump and Clinton  would have been the same could not be  more wrong obviously Hillary Clinton  would not have signed orders moving  forward on undi Dakota access and  Keystone XL hillary clinton would not  have ordered all references to climate  change be removed from the white house  and epa websites etc etc etc so on the  one hand you have the idea that most  everybody on the on the reasonable left  and even on the in the center and some  center-right people are saying  trainwreck the number one priority needs  to be to allow something like a trump  presidency never to happen again on the  other side you have somewhat of a  fracturing which I described from my  visit to the Boston women's March last  weekend which is that there are those on  the Left who say hey you know what the  identity politics ideas did not work to  prevent Trump from being elected and we  need to support minority groups not by  singular focus on individual minority  groups but by a broader anti-corruption  anteye kleptocratic economic message of  broader justice right and I don't know  which force is going to win I don't know  that I would call the left fractured  although I think that there are  differences of opinion on the left in  terms of what the next step needs to be  does that make sense  yeah I mean do you think that there  needs to be a strong vocal opinion  amongst maybe Center leftist that the  social justice warrior wing of the party  the the identity politics wing of the  party needs to be like definitively  rebuked within the parties no so I know  where you're going with this and I know  that there are people a lot of people  have been emailing me and talking to me  about David isn't it time for the left  to just denounce social justice warriors  for me when someone even uses the term  social justice warrior I already want to  know more about what they even mean by  that because it's become pejorative in a  way that I think goes above and beyond  sort of my criticisms of the identity  politics focus that sometimes exists so  I don't think the left needs to denounce  those who seek social justice I won't  even call them social justice warriors I  don't think it's about denouncing them I  think it's about having a pragmatic  conversation and saying hey if you're a  progressive you care about  discrimination against minority groups  you care about individuals who because  of their identity are disproportionately  negatively affected by policy or policy  be but from a pragmatic perspective  let's create a broader more broadly  appealing way to bring people together  for action that that's as far as I would  go and how I would delineate it well I  hope that can happen all right I hope so  to really appreciate the call always  great to hear from Los Angeles
 

